<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Alcīdes</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀλκείδης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a male descendant of
				Alceus;</i> usu. <i>his grandson Hercules</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				E. 7, 61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 8, 203</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
			321</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid memorem Alciden?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6, 123</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1, 12, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tib. 4, 1,
				12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 20, 49</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non fugis, Alcide,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					9, 75</span></i>
			; voc. also Alcidā, <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Fur. 1343</span></i>.</div>
